A_657 - In my opinion, animal milk and animal-derived foods are not compatible with our bodies, regardless of their flavor. They are particularly indigestible, and furthermore, I believe that if they were compatible with all the milk many people drank in their childhood, they should be as muscular as bulls. Instead, there is no muscle development proportional to the amount of milk drunk. Furthermore, it is important to know that animal milk is produced by mothers who are often impregnated artificially and is then taken from them, to the detriment of their babies. Furthermore, it is unclear why certain plant-based foods cannot be called "soy milk" or "rice milk" when in fact they are also liquid and the same color. No one has ever complained about peanut butter. Nor about the Milky Way.